id: blinding
name: Blinding
kind: battlefield
lightLevel: 2
source: Core Rule
description: >
  You cannot see. Halve your Awareness, Defense Value and Perception Skill Bonus.
text: >
  * Blinding (2). Halve your Awareness, Defense Value, and the Skill Bonus for your
  Perception Skill.

---

# Pitch Black's numbers at the other end of the table, for the same reason Bright repeats
# Dark.
#
# This is the one the Blinded Combat Condition names: "suffer from the effects of the
# Blinding Light Level, regardless of what the current Light Level is." Blinded writes the
# same three lines itself rather than reading this file, because it applies whatever the
# light is doing.
#
# Which means a Character who is Blinded while standing in Blinding light halves all three
# twice. Nothing in the rules says they do not, and two multiplications is what this engine
# does with two halvings - "a multiply is applied after all other modifications", and there
# are two of them.

[passive]
awareness *= 0.5;
defenseValue *= 0.5;
skill.perception.bonus *= 0.5;
